WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Evening comes, and over the
street the daylight slowly fades.

2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:09.180
Then, with nobody near it, the
street lamp switches itself on.

3
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:12.160
It has no eyes, and no one is watching it.

4
00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.850
So how can a circuit sense
that it is getting dark?

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.530
In this mission, you'll use a sliding
contact to tap off any voltage you choose

6
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.340
from a fixed supply.

7
00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:28.510
Then you'll put a 2.2 and a 3.3 kilo-ohm
resistor in series across 12 volts,

8
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.840
and find the voltage across each.

9
00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:35.180
Your mission: explain how the street
lamp's circuit senses that it is getting

10
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:35.790
dark.
